{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# KrishiRakshak — PlantVillage Crop Disease Classification\n",
    "## MobileNetV2 Transfer Learning Training\n",
    "\n",
    "**Problem Statement:** SIH26131 — Early Detection and Management of Crop Diseases and Pest Infestations\n",
    "\n",
    "**Dataset:** [PlantVillage Dataset (Kaggle)](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/abdallahalidev/plantvillage-dataset)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Instructions\n",
    "1. Upload this notebook to Kaggle\n",
    "2. Add the PlantVillage dataset as an input (via the Kaggle dataset search)\n",
    "3. Set GPU accelerator in notebook settings\n",
    "4. Run all cells top to bottom\n",
    "5. Download the exported model artifacts from the output"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Import Libraries"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "import tensorflow as tf\n",
    "from tensorflow import keras\n",
    "from tensorflow.keras import layers, models\n",
    "from tensorflow.keras.applications import MobileNetV2\n",
    "from tensorflow.keras.preprocessing.image import ImageDataGenerator\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import classification_report, confusion_matrix\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"TensorFlow version: {tf.__version__}\")\n",
    "print(f\"GPU available: {tf.config.list_physical_devices('GPU')}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Configure Dataset Path\n",
    "\n",
    "In Kaggle, datasets are typically available at `/kaggle/input/<dataset-name>/`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Detect Kaggle environment\n",
    "if os.path.exists('/kaggle/input'):\n",
    "    KAGGLE_MODE = True\n",
    "    # Update this path to match the actual dataset name in your Kaggle input\n",
    "    DATASET_ROOT = Path('/kaggle/input/plantvillage-dataset')\n",
    "    # The PlantVillage dataset has a 'plantvillage' subdirectory with 'dataset' inside\n",
    "    # Adjust this path based on actual structure\n",
    "    for candidate in [\n",
    "        DATASET_ROOT / 'plantvillage' / 'dataset',\n",
    "        DATASET_ROOT / 'dataset',\n",
    "        DATASET_ROOT,\n",
    "    ]:\n",
    "        if candidate.exists():\n",
    "            DATASET_ROOT = candidate\n",
    "            break\n",
    "    OUTPUT_DIR = Path('/kaggle/working')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    KAGGLE_MODE = False\n",
    "    DATASET_ROOT = Path('./plantvillage-dataset')\n",
    "    OUTPUT_DIR = Path('./output')\n",
    "    OUTPUT_DIR.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check if color or grayscale images\n",
    "COLOR_MODE = 'rgb'  # PlantVillage color images\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Kaggle mode: {KAGGLE_MODE}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Dataset root: {DATASET_ROOT}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Output dir: {OUTPUT_DIR}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# List directories to understand structure\n",
    "if DATASET_ROOT.exists():\n",
    "    print(\"\\nDataset contents:\")\n",
    "    for item in sorted(DATASET_ROOT.iterdir()):\n",
    "        print(f\"  {item.name}/\")\n",
    "        if item.is_dir():\n",
    "            sub = list(item.iterdir())[:3]\n",
    "            for s in sub:\n",
    "                print(f\"    {s.name}\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"WARNING: Dataset not found at {DATASET_ROOT}\")\n",
    "    print(\"Please add the PlantVillage dataset to your Kaggle notebook.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Configuration"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "IMG_SIZE = 224\n",
    "BATCH_SIZE = 32\n",
    "EPOCHS_HEAD = 10       # epochs for training classification head\n",
    "EPOCHS_FINETUNE = 5    # epochs for fine-tuning upper layers\n",
    "LEARNING_RATE_HEAD = 0.001\n",
    "LEARNING_RATE_FINETUNE = 1e-5\n",
    "VALIDATION_SPLIT = 0.15\n",
    "TEST_SPLIT = 0.1\n",
    "RANDOM_SEED = 42\n",
    "\n",
    "MODEL_SAVE_PATH = OUTPUT_DIR / 'plant_disease_model.keras'\n",
    "CLASS_NAMES_SAVE_PATH = OUTPUT_DIR / 'class_names.json'\n",
    "METRICS_SAVE_PATH = OUTPUT_DIR / 'training_metrics.json'\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Image size: {IMG_SIZE}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Batch size: {BATCH_SIZE}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Load and Inspect Classes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Find the actual image directories\n",
    "# PlantVillage typically has class folders directly or inside a 'color' subdirectory\n",
    "data_dir = None\n",
    "for candidate in [DATASET_ROOT, DATASET_ROOT / 'color', DATASET_ROOT / 'rgb']:\n",
    "    if candidate.exists():\n",
    "        dirs = [d for d in candidate.iterdir() if d.is_dir()]\n",
    "        if len(dirs) > 5:  # Looks like class directories\n",
    "            data_dir = candidate\n",
    "            break\n",
    "\n",
    "if data_dir is None:\n",
    "    raise ValueError(f\"Could not find class directories in {DATASET_ROOT}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "class_dirs = sorted([d.name for d in data_dir.iterdir() if d.is_dir()])\n",
    "num_classes = len(class_dirs)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Data directory: {data_dir}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Number of classes: {num_classes}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nClasses:\")\n",
    "for i, cls in enumerate(class_dirs):\n",
    "    count = len(list((data_dir / cls).glob('*.jpg'))) + len(list((data_dir / cls).glob('*.png')))\n",
    "    print(f\"  {i}: {cls} ({count} images)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Create Train / Validation / Test Datasets"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "datagen = ImageDataGenerator(\n",
    "    rescale=1./255,\n",
    "    validation_split=VALIDATION_SPLIT + TEST_SPLIT,\n",
    "    rotation_range=25,\n",
    "    width_shift_range=0.2,\n",
    "    height_shift_range=0.2,\n",
    "    shear_range=0.15,\n",
    "    zoom_range=0.2,\n",
n    "    horizontal_flip=True,\n",
    "    fill_mode='nearest'\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "test_datagen = ImageDataGenerator(rescale=1./255)\n",
    "\n",
    "train_generator = datagen.flow_from_directory(\n",
    "    data_dir,\n",
    "    target_size=(IMG_SIZE, IMG_SIZE),\n",
    "    batch_size=BATCH_SIZE,\n",
    "    class_mode='categorical',\n",
    "    subset='training',\n",
    "    seed=RANDOM_SEED,\n",
    "    color_mode=COLOR_MODE\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "val_test_datagen = ImageDataGenerator(\n",
    "    rescale=1./255,\n",
    "    validation_split=VALIDATION_SPLIT + TEST_SPLIT\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "val_generator = val_test_datagen.flow_from_directory(\n",
    "    data_dir,\n",
    "    target_size=(IMG_SIZE, IMG_SIZE),\n",
    "    batch_size=BATCH_SIZE,\n",
    "    class_mode='categorical',\n",
    "    subset='validation',\n",
    "    seed=RANDOM_SEED,\n",
    "    color_mode=COLOR_MODE\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "class_names = list(train_generator.class_indices.keys())\n",
    "print(f\"\\nTraining samples: {train_generator.samples}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Validation samples: {val_generator.samples}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Class names: {class_names}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Build MobileNetV2 Transfer Learning Model"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "base_model = MobileNetV2(\n",
    "    input_shape=(IMG_SIZE, IMG_SIZE, 3),\n",
    "    include_top=False,\n",
    "    weights='imagenet'\n",
    ")\n",
    "base_model.trainable = False\n",
    "\n",
    "model = models.Sequential([\n",
    "    base_model,\n",
    "    layers.GlobalAveragePooling2D(),\n",
    "    layers.BatchNormalization(),\n",
    "    layers.Dropout(0.3),\n",
    "    layers.Dense(256, activation='relu'),\n",
    "    layers.BatchNormalization(),\n",
    "    layers.Dropout(0.3),\n",
    "    layers.Dense(num_classes, activation='softmax')\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "model.compile(\n",
    "    optimizer=keras.optimizers.Adam(learning_rate=LEARNING_RATE_HEAD),\n",
    "    loss='categorical_crossentropy',\n",
    "    metrics=['accuracy']\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "model.summary()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Train Classification Head"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "callbacks_head = [\n",
    "    keras.callbacks.EarlyStopping(\n",
    "        monitor='val_accuracy',\n",
    "        patience=3,\n",
    "        restore_best_weights=True\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "    keras.callbacks.ReduceLROnPlateau(\n",
    "        monitor='val_loss',\n",
    "        factor=0.5,\n",
    "        patience=2,\n",
    "        min_lr=1e-7\n",
    "    )\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "history_head = model.fit(\n",
    "    train_generator,\n",
    "    epochs=EPOCHS_HEAD,\n",
    "    validation_data=val_generator,\n",
    "    callbacks=callbacks_head\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Fine-Tune Upper Layers of MobileNetV2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Unfreeze the top 30 layers of MobileNetV2\n",
    "base_model.trainable = True\n",
    "for layer in base_model.layers[:-30]:\n",
    "    layer.trainable = False\n",
    "\n",
    "model.compile(\n",
    "    optimizer=keras.optimizers.Adam(learning_rate=LEARNING_RATE_FINETUNE),\n",
    "    loss='categorical_crossentropy',\n",
    "    metrics=['accuracy']\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "callbacks_finetune = [\n",
    "    keras.callbacks.EarlyStopping(\n",
    "        monitor='val_accuracy',\n",
    "        patience=3,\n",
    "        restore_best_weights=True\n",
    "    )\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "history_finetune = model.fit(\n",
    "    train_generator,\n",
    "    epochs=EPOCHS_FINETUNE,\n",
    "    validation_data=val_generator,\n",
    "    callbacks=callbacks_finetune\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Evaluate on Validation Data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "val_loss, val_accuracy = model.evaluate(val_generator)\n",
    "print(f\"\\nValidation Accuracy: {val_accuracy:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Validation Loss: {val_loss:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Generate predictions and classification report\n",
    "val_generator.reset()\n",
    "Y_pred = model.predict(val_generator)\n",
    "y_pred = np.argmax(Y_pred, axis=1)\n",
    "y_true = val_generator.classes\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nClassification Report:\")\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_true, y_pred, target_names=class_names))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Confusion Matrix\n",
    "cm = confusion_matrix(y_true, y_pred)\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 10))\n",
    "sns.heatmap(cm, annot=True, fmt='d', cmap='Blues',\n",
    "            xticklabels=class_names, yticklabels=class_names)\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Predicted')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Actual')\n",
    "plt.title('Confusion Matrix')\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=90, fontsize=8)\n",
    "plt.yticks(rotation=0, fontsize=8)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(OUTPUT_DIR / 'confusion_matrix.png', dpi=150)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Plot Training History"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def plot_history(history_list, titles):\n",
    "    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for history, title in zip(history_list, titles):\n",
    "        axes[0].plot(history.history['accuracy'], label=f'{title} Train')\n",
    "        axes[0].plot(history.history['val_accuracy'], label=f'{title} Val')\n",
    "        axes[1].plot(history.history['loss'], label=f'{title} Train')\n",
    "        axes[1].plot(history.history['val_loss'], label=f'{title} Val')\n",
    "    \n",
    "    axes[0].set_title('Accuracy')\n",
    "    axes[0].set_xlabel('Epoch')\n",
    "    axes[0].set_ylabel('Accuracy')\n",
    "    axes[0].legend()\n",
    "    axes[0].grid(True)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    axes[1].set_title('Loss')\n",
    "    axes[1].set_xlabel('Epoch')\n",
    "    axes[1].set_ylabel('Loss')\n",
    "    axes[1].legend()\n",
    "    axes[1].grid(True)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.savefig(OUTPUT_DIR / 'training_history.png', dpi=150)\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "plot_history([history_head, history_finetune], ['Head', 'Fine-tune'])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 11. Save Model and Class Mapping"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "model.save(MODEL_SAVE_PATH)\n",
    "print(f\"Model saved to {MODEL_SAVE_PATH}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "class_names_list = list(train_generator.class_indices.keys())\n",
    "with open(CLASS_NAMES_SAVE_PATH, 'w') as f:\n",
    "    json.dump(class_names_list, f, indent=2)\n",
    "print(f\"Class names saved to {CLASS_NAMES_SAVE_PATH}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save training metrics\n",
    "metrics = {\n",
    "    \"val_accuracy\": float(val_accuracy),\n",
    "    \"val_loss\": float(val_loss),\n",
    "    \"num_classes\": num_classes,\n",
    "    \"class_names\": class_names_list,\n",
    "    \"img_size\": IMG_SIZE,\n",
    "    \"model_architecture\": \"MobileNetV2 + custom classification head\",\n",
    "    \"training_epochs_head\": EPOCHS_HEAD,\n",
    "    \"training_epochs_finetune\": EPOCHS_FINETUNE\n",
    "}\n",
    "with open(METRICS_SAVE_PATH, 'w') as f:\n",
    "    json.dump(metrics, f, indent=2)\n",
    "print(f\"Metrics saved to {METRICS_SAVE_PATH}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 12. Download Instructions\n",
    "\n",
    "After training completes:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Go to the **Output** panel on the right side of the Kaggle notebook\n",
    "2. You will find:\n",
    "   - `plant_disease_model.keras` — the trained model\n",
    "   - `class_names.json` — class label mapping\n",
    "   - `training_metrics.json` — accuracy, loss, and configuration\n",
    "   - `confusion_matrix.png` — confusion matrix visualization\n",
    "   - `training_history.png` — accuracy/loss curves\n",
    "3. Download all files\n",
    "4. Place `plant_disease_model.keras` and `class_names.json` into `ml-service/models/` in your KrishiRakshak project\n",
    "5. Set `MODEL_MODE=real` in your `ml-service/.env`\n",
    "6. Restart the ML service"
   ]
  }
